  "title": "A countable family of IMReps with finite total mass is represented by one IMRep",
  "statement": "Let P, n ∈ ℕ, U ⊆ ℝ^P open, and R_i = (M_i, θ_i, ξ_i) (i ∈ ℕ) IMReps in U with Σ_i μ_{R_i}(U) < ∞, where μ_R := θ·Hⁿ⌞M is IMRep.measure. Then there is an IMRep R' in U such that for every test form ω ∈ 𝒟ⁿ(U) the real series Σ_i R_i.action(ω) has sum R'.action(ω) (HasSum). Here R.action(ω) = ∫_M θ(x)·ξ(x)(ω(x)) dHⁿ(x).",
  "lean_statement": "∀ (P n : ℕ) (U : Set (Euclid P)) (R : ℕ → IMRep U n), IsOpen U → ∑' i, (R i).measure U ≠ ∞ → ∃ R' : IMRep U n, ∀ ω : TestFormOn U n, HasSum (fun i => (R i).action (ω : DifferentialForm (Euclid P) n)) (R'.action (ω : DifferentialForm (Euclid P) n))",
